data 453
docs(perf): playlist scroll jank root-cause analysis + optimization plan

Documents the 40fps scroll investigation and the 5-task optimization
roadmap for playlist_page.dart:

P0-1 (this commit): scroll offset ValueNotifier (done)
P0-2 (this commit): filter result cache (done)
P1    : flexibleSpace RepaintBoundary isolation (pending)
P2    : AnimatedContainer drop + provider-watch narrowing (optional)
P2    : artwork prefetch defer 150ms (optional)
from :972
commit refs/heads/rust-local-force
mark :974
author Little-White3110 <Little-White3110@users.noreply.github.com> 1788054986 +0800
committer Little-White3110 <Little-White3110@users.noreply.github.com> 1788054986 +0800
data 808
perf(playlist): cache flexibleSpace subtree and isolate its repaint

flexibleSpace content does not depend on scroll offset, but the
SliverAppBar rebuilds every frame while scrolling (background lerp +
title fade-in driven by ValueListenableBuilder), re-building the whole
flexibleSpace subtree (140x140 cover, gradient, wallpaper) each frame.

- _buildCachedFlexibleSpace() caches the widget instance keyed by
  name / artwork / creator / songCount / useBackgroundImage /
  colorScheme; the identical instance makes updateChild skip the
  whole subtree rebuild during scroll.
- Wrapped in RepaintBoundary so scroll repaints only the app-bar
  background layer, not the static header content.

Static: flutter analyze clean (no new error/warning).
Verified: builds 31s, install -r Success, App starts clean.
from :973
commit refs/heads/rust-local-force
mark :975
author Little-White3110 <Little-White3110@users.noreply.github.com> 1788055417 +0800
committer Little-White3110 <Little-White3110@users.noreply.github.com> 1788055417 +0800
data 918
perf(artwork): decode list-item covers as thumbnails (cacheWidth)

SmartArtworkImage / LocalArtworkImage loaded covers without cacheWidth,
so every 400x400 artwork (kugou_provider._stripArtworkUrl substitutes
{size}->400) was fully decoded even though list items display at ~52px
(~6.6x pixel waste). 400x400 bitmaps (~640KB each) also blow past the
ImageCache 100MB limit on long playlists, evicting entries and forcing
network re-fetch + re-decode on scroll-back.

- decodeWidth = (size * devicePixelRatio).round().clamp(32, 480) computed
  once in build; passed to every Image.network / Image.memory / Image.file
  branch (isFill/fullscreen cases pass null).
- cacheWidth participates in the ImageCache key, so the same URL at the
  same size shares a single decoded bitmap across all list rows.

Static: flutter analyze clean (no new issue).
Verified: builds 29s, install -r Success, App starts clean (pid 18607).
from :974
